From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:27:18 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): add the local folder to the file manager's
 Places

Motivation: on KDE the synchronized folder is reached only through
DriveSync's own menu; Dolphin, the Places panel and every KDE file dialog
list the places of $XDG_DATA_HOME/user-places.xbel, where the folder is
missing.

Changes: the account menu offers "Add local folder to Places" where that
file exists. The action appends one XBEL bookmark (the freedesktop.org icon
extension when the file declares it, KDE's ID and isSystemItem metadata)
before the closing element, keeps the rest of the file byte for byte,
replaces it atomically, and never adds the same folder twice. It runs only
when the person chooses it.

Validation: cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy -D warnings, a unit test for
escaping, idempotence and preservation; in a Plasma session Dolphin shows
the entry under Places after the action.

Limitations: overlay icons per file in Dolphin would need a file-state
interface from the engine and a KOverlayIconPlugin; not part of this
change.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5)
Origin: vendor, Sparky Stereo OS (branch order299 of the edition's DriveSync fork)
Forwarded: no
